{"game": "roboquest", "language": "english", "appid": 692890, "month": "2023-05", "window": 3, "start_date": 1684195200, "end_date": 1684886399, "month_true_total": 87, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-03 01:52:04 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "138810041", "author": {"steamid": "76561198170006033", "personaname": "Allegaeon", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198170006033/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 6, "playtime_forever": 5262, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 4639, "last_played": 1733754461, "avatar": "a7b0b2ff4ac22e026f3e77b6c5b0d97744f85b85"}, "language": "english", "review": "It's like doom, but instead of an atmospheric hellscape full of gore, you get cartoony robots. And its damn good. The core gameplay is fast and satisfying, and the rouglike aspects keep things interesting. Good game", "timestamp_created": 1684812980, "timestamp_updated": 1717474246, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1597939791", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "138716630", "author": {"steamid": "76561198036629241", "personaname": "ﾚのひ刀ﾑ丂", "persona_status": "in-game", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Lounas/", "num_games_owned": 2105, "num_reviews": 14635, "playtime_forever": 1542, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 228, "last_played": 1710485914, "avatar": "92b512dd2a789fe359493d2b6798ad129d3852d5"}, "language": "english", "review": "⠀", "timestamp_created": 1684702328, "timestamp_updated": 1684702328, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 10, "votes_funny": 7, "weighted_vote_score": "0.607532203197479248", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1597939791", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "138712714", "author": {"steamid": "76561199084120042", "personaname": "Machewy", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/machewy_L/", "num_games_owned": 94, "num_reviews": 9, "playtime_forever": 6500, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 4097, "last_played": 1764212588, "avatar": "4e4c8c7173069beec5df4fc8743281c15a8304f1"}, "language": "english", "review": "I've stumbled upon many games I'd consider hidden gems, and Roboquest undoubtedly falls into that category. Let me be frank; its replayability surpasses that of any FPS I've played in quite some time. Sure, there are rough patches, like the grind for data-logs, but trust me, it's worth it. Those logs add depth to the later stages, making the journey all the more rewarding.\r\nNow, about those puzzles. Some argue that if you're resorting to YouTube for a solution, they should be optional. But not here. Pay attention during your runs, and you'll see how everything ties together – the lore, the logs, the doors, the crystals – it's all part of a stellar story.\r\nI struggle to find the right words; Roboquest nails the movement shooter formula. If I had to nitpick, adding a PvP mode would take it to the next level. Picture this: a race to defeat Iris, with real-time updates on your opponent's progress. Or how about a 5v5 mode, objective-based like Valorant or CS: GO?\r\nIn summary, Roboquest has me hooked, and I can't wait to see what the devs have in store next.", "timestamp_created": 1684698613, "timestamp_updated": 1715146688, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1597939791", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "138655606", "author": {"stea